# GGMI Mexico: Reducing Media Weight Now, Ramping Ahead of November

**Entity:** GGMI, GAIN Global Markets Inc. (Mexico, forex.com/es)
**Prepared for:** FOREX.com
**Prepared by:** brlvnt
**Date:** August 27, 2026
**Measured against:** Approved August 2026 monthly budget by channel (FOREX.com tracker, last updated 08/06/2026)
**Status:** DRAFT for FOREX.com review. Not for distribution.

---

## 1. Executive recommendation

FOREX.com is spending almost all of the August budget. The problem is which channels receive it.

Bing produces a submitted application for $379 and is running at 62% of its approved budget. Azerion produces one for $978, has become more expensive every month since April, and is running at 123% of its approved budget. Native produces none and is running at 115%. The program funds its weakest channel above budget and its strongest below.

brlvnt recommends the **Controlled Pullback: $61,000 a month, a 51% reduction against the approved $125,000.** On current costs per application it delivers about the same number of applications as August does today, for half the money. A **Deep Pullback at $33,500** is the alternative if cash preservation outweighs volume.

Hold the reduced level through September and October. The decision to ramp back up should be taken in the first half of October, not in September, because the concentration of market-moving events runs from late October into mid-November and media needs lead time to be in position for it.

