## 8. When to ramp back up

The reduced level should hold through September and October. The ramp decision is taken in the first half of October, and money starts moving in the second half.

That timing is set by how long each channel takes to reach efficient delivery, not by the calendar alone.

| Channel | Lead time to full weight | Start by |
|---|---|---|
| Quantcast and other programmatic | Three to four weeks to rebuild modelled audiences and clear the learning period; longer from a standing start | Early to mid October |
| Azerion display | Insertion order plus a comparable ramp | Early to mid October |
| Bing search | Days, since intent is captured at the moment of search | Late October |

Search can be raised close to the event. Everything above it cannot. A programmatic audience started on November 1 is still learning while the November 3 window is happening, which is the specific outcome both options above are shaped to avoid.

**Recommended sequence**

1. **September.** Hold the reduced level. Read the September 15 to 16 FOMC and the September 24 Banco de México decision as information. Take no budget action.
2. **First half of October.** Decide the ramp. The inputs are one full month of the reallocation, whether Bing held its cost per application at its new weight, whether the reduced Azerion line improved, and whether MXN CVOL and FX volumes have started to move.
3. **Second half of October.** Begin rebuilding upper funnel if the decision is to ramp, so audiences are in efficient delivery before November 3.
4. **Late October into November.** Scale Bing toward and beyond its approved weight, sized to the demand actually appearing rather than to the forecast.
5. **Mid-November onward.** Read the post-election and post-Banco de México period, then set the level for December and the new fiscal year.

A note on the fiscal boundary. The approved plan in the tracker runs to September, which closes FY26. October onward carries no approved figure. The ramp decision in early October and FY27 planning are therefore the same conversation, and we would rather bring a recommendation to it built on two months of evidence from the reallocation than on an August that everyone agrees was quiet.

