## 9. September

The approved September budget is $205,000, an increase of about 64% on August. Three of its lines are not currently running.

| Line | Approved September | Status |
|---|---:|---|
| Bing | $30,000 | Active, the strongest performer |
| Quantcast | $35,000 | Active |
| Azerion | $35,000 | Active, at 123% of its August budget and $978 per application |
| Native | $25,000 | Active, no attributed applications |
| Meta | $30,000 | Paused |
| TikTok | $10,000 | Never run for GGMI this fiscal year |
| Strategic Partnerships | $40,000 | Not currently running |
| **Total** | **$205,000** | |

**We do not recommend the September plan as approved.** Eighty thousand dollars of it, or 39%, is allocated to three channels that are not live, two of which have no GGMI performance history to size against. Committing that while applications are not funding, while the strongest channel sits below its approved budget, and while the largest channel gets more expensive every month, is difficult to defend on current evidence.

We recommend running September at the chosen option, $61,000 or $33,500, and holding the same level through October. The $80,000 across Meta, TikTok and Strategic Partnerships should be deferred rather than cancelled, so it stays available for the October ramp if the evidence supports launching those channels then.

